# The fourth road panel (TSC_Road_Quiet check spot, Insight 14). The
# winter road: the rider who died at the gate, and the instruction the
# Quiet Brothers followed eight centuries later, sight unseen.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_RoadQuiet

== start ==
The fourth panel reads easily at the top and gets harder the further down it goes, and it is not the carving that resists. It is what the carving means.

A rider in winter, reaching a walled house with a bell tower. The rider dying at the gate, taken in too late.

* [Read what is underneath.] -> under

== under ==
Underneath, the house again: gate barred, bell rope cut, and the brothers filing into their wall niches in order, smallest to largest, like a household putting itself away.

These are not memorial scenes. They are steps. Not what happened: what *will* happen.

* "The monastery did all of it. Eight hundred years later." -> did

== did ==
Barred gate. Cut rope. The brothers in their niches, in order. The party walked through the proof of it and read the songbook in the house that obeyed.

The Quiet Brothers never saw this wall. What reached them is what reached Wren: unfinished work, still moving, and it does not stop until its instructions are carried out.

* [Move on.] -> end
